1
00:00:04,398 --> 00:00:10,936
TH: Before we start, does anyone have a charger I can borrow after this? Mine has given up.

2
00:00:12,458 --> 00:00:17,073
LUCAS MARTIN: I've got a spare in my bag. Remind me after the call.

3
00:00:18,527 --> 00:00:20,834
TH: You're a hero. Okay, let's begin.

4
00:00:21,189 --> 00:00:28,496
KENJI WATANABE: I spent a day on chart rendering. Big dashboards are slow on older phones, so we need some sampling.

5
00:00:28,895 --> 00:00:37,356
TH: I had a quick call about the tablet layout this morning. We're aligned, I'd love a second pair of eyes on it.

6
00:00:38,494 --> 00:00:41,186
LUCAS MARTIN: Where are we with the login screen?

7
00:00:42,182 --> 00:00:46,028
KENJI WATANABE: It's nearly ready for review. I'm reasonably happy with it.

8
00:00:46,584 --> 00:00:52,353
TH: I reopened the store screenshots because something looked off. It's mostly done again, nothing dramatic.

9
00:00:53,711 --> 00:01:00,249
KENJI WATANABE: Quick update on the build pipeline. It's further along than I expected. Honestly, it should be fine.

10
00:01:00,718 --> 00:01:07,256
TH: Not much from me this week. Mostly the beta feedback queue. That work is about halfway there.

11
00:01:08,343 --> 00:01:13,727
KENJI WATANABE: We added a simple in-app feedback form. It sends straight into the support queue.

12
00:01:14,088 --> 00:01:23,318
ANANYA R.: Okay, launch readiness. We're close to the date we set at the replanning session, so I want a clear picture. Kenji, where are we?

13
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:32,429
KENJI WATANABE: Mixed. iOS is in great shape. It passed store review on the first try, and the crash-free rate is well above our bar.

14
00:01:33,455 --> 00:01:34,608
LUCAS MARTIN: That's great news.

15
00:01:35,628 --> 00:01:46,781
KENJI WATANABE: Android is the problem. The crash that happens when the app returns from the background is still there. Grace can reproduce it now, which helps, but it's not fixed.

16
00:01:47,905 --> 00:01:50,212
ANANYA R.: How bad is it in numbers?

17
00:01:51,335 --> 00:02:02,873
KENJI WATANABE: The Android build has a 2.4% crash rate on the beta right now. That's far below the crash-free bar we set. If we launched today, store reviews would hammer us.

18
00:02:03,963 --> 00:02:13,963
TH: And the fix isn't trivial. It's in how we restore state when the app comes back. We need to restructure part of the chart loading code.

19
00:02:15,288 --> 00:02:22,980
LUCAS MARTIN: Push notifications work on my test devices. I want to try a wider range of phones before I trust it.

20
00:02:24,162 --> 00:02:28,777
KENJI WATANABE: Tomás, you mentioned the accessibility fixes earlier in the week. Any news?

21
00:02:29,948 --> 00:02:35,717
TH: Some. It's basically finished, apart from tidying up, it took longer than it should have.

22
00:02:37,061 --> 00:02:37,961
KENJI WATANABE: Perfect.

23
00:02:38,866 --> 00:02:46,173
TH: Small thing from me. I picked up the crash dashboard again the end of last week. It's mostly done.

24
00:02:47,734 --> 00:02:51,580
ANANYA R.: Who's looking at the app permissions prompt at the moment?

25
00:02:52,570 --> 00:02:55,262
TH: Me, mostly. It's nearly ready for review.

26
00:02:55,851 --> 00:03:02,774
KENJI WATANABE: I made decent progress on the alert settings screen this morning. It's basically finished, apart from tidying up.

27
00:03:03,899 --> 00:03:11,206
TH: Not much from me this week. Mostly the chart renderer. That work is basically finished, apart from tidying up.

28
00:03:12,794 --> 00:03:15,486
KENJI WATANABE: Is the store screenshots still on track?

29
00:03:16,790 --> 00:03:22,174
TH: Roughly. It's in decent shape, I'd love a second pair of eyes on it.

30
00:03:22,973 --> 00:03:24,896
KENJI WATANABE: Nice. Thanks for the update.

31
00:03:25,179 --> 00:03:31,332
LUCAS MARTIN: I tested on a really old tablet over the weekend. It works, but it's not pretty.

32
00:03:32,895 --> 00:03:37,125
KENJI WATANABE: Some older Android phones render the fonts slightly differently. Mostly cosmetic.

33
00:03:37,507 --> 00:03:40,583
ANANYA R.: Could we launch iOS first and Android later?

34
00:03:41,852 --> 00:03:51,082
LUCAS MARTIN: From marketing, I'd really rather not. Half our customers are on Android. A split launch means two campaigns and a lot of confused people.

35
00:03:51,357 --> 00:03:57,126
KENJI WATANABE: And from engineering, it's one app. Splitting the launch doubles the support load for weeks.

36
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:05,067
TH: From a leadership point of view, the main thing I need is confidence in the dates and the risks.

37
00:04:05,652 --> 00:04:11,805
KENJI WATANABE: If anything changes, I'd rather hear it early in a message than late in a meeting.

38
00:04:12,778 --> 00:04:20,470
LUCAS MARTIN: Login with the existing accounts works. The password reset flow still opens the web page, which is fine for now.

39
00:04:21,418 --> 00:04:26,033
TH: I'll share these slides afterwards for anyone who wants to forward them.

40
00:04:27,524 --> 00:04:32,524
KENJI WATANABE: Accessibility pass is next. Font scaling breaks a couple of screens right now.

41
00:04:32,815 --> 00:04:38,584
TH: I'll keep this at a high level and we can go deeper wherever people want.

42
00:04:39,235 --> 00:04:43,850
KENJI WATANABE: Tomás, did you get a chance to look at the crash dashboard?

43
00:04:44,766 --> 00:04:48,227
TH: Not yet, sorry. It's on my list for Thursday.

44
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:55,628
KENJI WATANABE: We found a memory leak on the dashboard list screen. It's fixed on a branch, waiting for review.

45
00:04:56,468 --> 00:05:14,160
ANANYA R.: Then we move the date again. I don't like it, but launching with a known crash bug is worse. The mobile launch moves to May 27, both stores, same day. That gives Kenji time to fix the Android crash-rate bug and Grace time to verify it.

46
00:05:14,450 --> 00:05:21,373
LUCAS MARTIN: Okay. May 27. I'll move the campaign. I'd rather move it once more than launch something people hate.

47
00:05:22,953 --> 00:05:29,106
TH: Same rules apply. Crash-free bar, zero blockers, QA sign-off. The date only holds if those pass.

48
00:05:30,499 --> 00:05:35,114
KENJI WATANABE: Understood. I'll give daily updates on the Android fix in the channel.

49
00:05:36,462 --> 00:05:42,615
ANANYA R.: Quick aside, the building is testing the fire alarm tomorrow morning, so expect noise during calls.

50
00:05:43,381 --> 00:05:46,457
KENJI WATANABE: Thanks for the warning. I'll schedule nothing important.

51
00:05:46,794 --> 00:05:47,694
ANANYA R.: Okay, continuing.

52
00:05:48,496 --> 00:05:55,034
TH: Heads up, I'll need someone to review the deep link handling soon. It's slower than I hoped.

53
00:05:56,519 --> 00:05:59,211
LUCAS MARTIN: Is anyone blocked on the dashboard list?

54
00:06:00,183 --> 00:06:03,644
KENJI WATANABE: Not blocked, just slow. It's slower than I hoped.

55
00:06:04,388 --> 00:06:07,849
ANANYA R.: Thanks, that's clear. Let's go through the open questions.

56
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:13,925
KENJI WATANABE: Tomás, did you get a chance to look at the release checklist?

57
00:06:14,183 --> 00:06:18,413
TH: Not yet, sorry. It's on my list for first thing tomorrow.

58
00:06:18,844 --> 00:06:21,920
LUCAS MARTIN: Did the alert settings screen ever get reviewed?

59
00:06:23,507 --> 00:06:30,430
TH: I reviewed it after lunch yesterday. It's nearly ready for review, it took longer than it should have.

60
00:06:30,731 --> 00:06:35,731
KENJI WATANABE: Leadership mainly wants to know if anything needs their help. Is there anything?

61
00:06:37,295 --> 00:06:45,371
TH: On my side, work on the beta feedback queue is slower than I hoped. It took longer than it should have.

62
00:06:45,671 --> 00:06:53,363
LUCAS MARTIN: Can we talk about what we tell the beta testers and the waiting customers? They've already heard about one delay.

63
00:06:54,472 --> 00:06:55,372
ANANYA R.: Right.

64
00:06:56,856 --> 00:07:03,009
KENJI WATANABE: I'll write to the testers myself. They know about the crash, they've seen it. They'll understand.

65
00:07:03,259 --> 00:07:06,720
LUCAS MARTIN: And the customers who signed up for launch news?

66
00:07:08,185 --> 00:07:15,877
ANANYA R.: A short, honest message. We found a bug that would have made the experience worse, so we're fixing it first.

67
00:07:17,143 --> 00:07:21,758
LUCAS MARTIN: I'll draft it today and send it to you both for review.

68
00:07:22,779 --> 00:07:32,779
TH: From engineering, I'd like to move one person from the onboarding work to help Kenji for a couple of weeks. The chart loading code is tricky.

69
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:36,632
ANANYA R.: Is onboarding at risk if you do?

70
00:07:36,936 --> 00:07:44,628
TH: Not really. That team is in the polish phase, and the person I'm thinking of knows the chart code best.

71
00:07:45,519 --> 00:07:49,749
ANANYA R.: Then do it. The mobile fix is the priority right now.

72
00:07:50,512 --> 00:07:52,819
KENJI WATANABE: Thank you. That helps a lot.

73
00:07:54,334 --> 00:08:03,180
ANANYA R.: One more thing. I want this to be the last move. If the fix looks risky, tell me early, not the week before.

74
00:08:04,298 --> 00:08:05,198
LUCAS MARTIN: Sure.

75
00:08:05,591 --> 00:08:10,975
KENJI WATANABE: Will do. Honestly, I'm fairly confident. We know exactly where the bug is now.

76
00:08:11,426 --> 00:08:14,887
LUCAS MARTIN: Let's wrap there. Kenji, can you stop the recording?

77
00:08:16,271 --> 00:08:18,194
KENJI WATANABE: Stopping it now. Thanks, everyone.
